"On a bugfix branch Fix local startup in the `Development/waldorf-community-task-manager` project using the AI-DLC workflow.\n\nFollowing the README instructions revealed two issues:\n\n1. The machine defaults to Node `26.10.0`, while the project requires Node 24.x and npm 11.x. Compatible versions are already installed through Homebrew at `/opt/homebrew/opt/node@24/bin`: Node `24.21.0` and npm `11.19.0`. The `nvm` command is unavailable.\n2. The `scripts/validate-runtime-config.ts` script, executed by `predev`, validates only `process.env` without loading `.env.local`. Startup therefore fails with `CONFIG_RUNTIME_MODE_INVALID: invalid APP_RUNTIME_MODE` before Next.js can load the configuration.\n\nThe current temporary workaround is:\n\n```bash\nexport PATH=\"/opt/homebrew/opt/node@24/bin:$PATH\"\nexport APP_RUNTIME_MODE=synthetic\nnpm run dev\n```\n\nExpected outcome:\n\n- Update the README with accurate instructions for selecting the supported Node/npm versions, including how to use an existing Homebrew Node 24 installation when nvm is unavailable.\n- Make `npm run dev` work with the documented local configuration without requiring a separate `APP_RUNTIME_MODE` export.\n- Investigate the same configuration-loading issue in `prebuild` and `prestart`, and fix affected startup commands consistently.\n- Preserve the Node 24.x/npm 11.x requirements and invalid-configuration checks.\n- Do not log secrets or connect to external or production systems.\n- Do not modify global machine or shell settings; document any necessary setup steps.\n\nFollow the project's AI-DLC approval checkpoints. Verify configuration loading and the documented local startup procedure, then summarize the changes and verification results."
